# Local settings for the build scripts: build.py at the root, and in examples/harmony/,
# examples/desktop/ and examples/android/ -- and for third/sync.py, which clones the engine
# sources into the same paths the builds read. Copy to .env, which git ignores,
# and uncomment what this machine needs. Android reads its SDK from
# examples/android/local.properties, and only the vcpkg and engine sources from here.
#
# A line here wins over the same name in the environment, such as the
# VULKAN_SDK or CUDA_PATH an installer sets. YOAI_<NAME> in the environment
# wins over this file, for one run.
#
# Format: NAME=VALUE, no spaces around `=`, # for comments, and a value may be
# wrapped in double quotes; an empty value reads as unset. Nothing is
# expanded, so write paths out in full. Only the names below are read;
# anything else here is left to other tools.

# --- Toolchain ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Visual Studio install root. Windows only.
#VS_DIR=C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community

# ninja.exe. Windows only; default is the one bundled with Visual Studio.
#NINJA=

# vcpkg checkout, where every build gets curl and OpenSSL. Default is
# third/vcpkg, cloned on the first run at vcpkg.json's builtin-baseline.
#VCPKG_ROOT=

# A host Vulkan SDK, for text-to-speech on the GPU: root `tts`, desktop `qtts`
# and harmony `vulkan`. Default is the VULKAN_SDK the LunarG installer sets.
# Root `tts` builds without it, for the CPU, and warns.
#VULKAN_SDK=

# A CUDA Toolkit, for text-to-speech on an NVIDIA GPU: root `tts` only, beside
# Vulkan. Default is the CUDA_PATH the Windows installer sets, then nvcc on
# PATH, then /usr/local/cuda. Root `tts` builds without it and says nothing.
#CUDA_PATH=

# --- Engine sources ----------------------------------------------------------
# `python third/sync.py clone` fetches these at the pinned commits, patched,
# into third/<name>. Most machines set nothing here: each setting points one
# checkout somewhere else -- a branch of your own, a newer upstream to try.

# llama.cpp: root `asr`, desktop and harmony `llama`, and root `tts` and
# `qtts` for its ggml. A bare root build fetches it on its first run.
#LLAMA_SRC=

# qwentts.cpp, for root `tts` and for `qtts`. A bare root build fetches it on
# its first run.
#QTTS_SRC=

# The two below are optional: evaluation lanes, built only when named, and
# fetched by nothing until you run `python third/sync.py clone <name>`.

# cosyvoice.cpp, for the CosyVoice3 CLI: `python build.py cosyvoice`.
#COSYVOICE_SRC=

# MNN, for the Qwen2.5-Omni lane: `mnn` in examples/desktop/ and
# examples/harmony/.
#MNN_SRC=
